  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. glass exports were $5.84B in 2025 (−4.2%) and $3.97B in January–August 2026 (+1.2%). Vehicle rear-view mirrors ($1.59B) and fiberglass (7019, $1.42B) make up over half.",
    "Canada has charged a 50% surtax on U.S. glass bottles, jars and other glass containers (7010.90.00) since September 8, 2026, CUSMA or not. Canadian food and beverage packers and manufacturers can claim it back.",
    "China charges 30% on U.S. rear-view mirrors and 35% on cast, rolled and float glass sheet unless the importer holds an exclusion. The exclusions end December 31, 2026 and the suspension of 24 points of China's extra duty ends January 10, 2027.",
    "The EU has charged 0% on every U.S. glass product since July 1, 2026 (normally up to 11%). Mexico, the top fiberglass buyer, charges 0% on goods that qualify for USMCA."
  ],
